course: dictionary
lesson: 11576
title: Announced: telling everyone
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Announced is the past form of announce. When someone announces something, they tell a lot of people an important piece of news, often officially or loudly. «The head teacher announced the winners at assembly.» Everyone in the hall heard the news at the same time.
explain: Announce can also mean saying something in a firm or surprising way. «"I'm leaving," she announced.» Nobody needed a news board for this. Mia simply said it clearly, so everyone noticed. Ask yourself: is this a big official message, or a firm, surprising statement?
explain: Sometimes announced means showing that something is coming. «Thunder announced the storm.» The thunder did not make a speech, but it gave a clear sign that the storm was on its way. The words around it tell you which meaning to use.
fact: Announced is the past form of announce.
fact: «Announced» can mean told many people something important, often officially or loudly.
fact: «"I'm leaving," she announced.» means she said it in a firm or surprising way.
fact: «Thunder announced the storm.» means the thunder showed that the storm was coming.
fact: Useful phrases: «it was announced that…», «announced the winner», «announced over the loudspeaker».
exercise: «The head teacher announced the winners at assembly.» What does announced mean here? | Lost the winners' names | Sang a quiet song | * Told everyone an important piece of news | Ate a big lunch
exercise: «"I'm going swimming," Sam announced.» What does this tell us about how Sam spoke? | * Firmly, so everyone noticed | He did not say a word | Sadly, with his head down | Very softly, almost in a whisper
exercise: In «Thunder announced the storm», which word means showed that the storm was coming? | * Announced | Storm | Thunder
test: What is the past form of announce? | Announces | Announcer | Announcing | * Announced
test: «The news was announced over the loudspeaker.» Where was the news shared? | In a shoe | On the moon | Under the desk | * Over the loudspeaker
exam: «The mayor announced the new park to the whole town.» What does announced mean? | Hid the news from everyone | Painted the gate | * Told the whole town officially | Forgot to tell anyone
